- Hard: none.

## Open questions

- Vector vs. raster for the QR fill: Pocket (vector) makes a milled QR with cleanly-sided modules. Raster (Child 12) makes a laser-burned QR. Engrave (single-line per module edge) makes a outlined QR. All three are useful; expose via the dropdown.
- Multiple QRs in one project: each one its own VcObject set on its own layer, or all on a shared "QR" layer? Shared layer simpler; per-QR layer cleaner. Pick shared, file follow-up if users complain.

